c_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":1.0,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.03266380236624941,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":22.4,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06048426458203038,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":78.3,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.016093404859577155,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":73.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.13822,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":92.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Sinclair, Inc., a media company, provides content on local television stations and digital platforms in the United States. It operates through two segments, Local Media and Tennis. The Local Media segment operates broadcast television stations, original networks, and content; provides free over-the-air programming and live local sporting events on its stations; distributes its content to multi-channel video programming distributors in exchange for contractual fees; and produces local and original news programs. This segment operates The Nest, a free over-the-air national broadcast TV network; Comet, a science fiction network; CHARGE!, an adventure and action-based network; The National News Desk, a news program; and Full Measure with Sharyl Attkisson, an investigative and political analysis program, as well as podcasts related to soccer and sports programming. Its Tennis segment offers Tennis Channel, a cable network that includes coverage of tennis' top tournaments and original professional sports, and tennis lifestyle shows; Tennis Channel International and Tennis Channel streaming services; Tennischannel 2, a 24-hours a day free ad-supported streaming television channel; Tennis.com; and FAST Channel Pickleballtv. The company also provides non-broadcast digital and internet solutions; and technical sales and services, including the design and manufacture of broadcast systems. In addition, it owns various investments in non-media related companies. The company distributes its content through its broadcast platform and third-party platforms that consist of programming provided by third-party networks and syndicators, local news, sports, and other original programming. The company was founded in 1971 and is headquartered in Hunt Valley, Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher S. Ripley | President & CEO | Age 48 | Compensation: $4.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $446K ranks in the below the sector median among Communication Services peers. Each employee generates $16K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Sinclair, Inc. is a small-cap communication services business with a $1.1B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +8.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $115M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 14% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (25.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.09169768667849605},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $11.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Communication Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["16 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Sinclair Inc. (SBGI) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/34/How_Sinclair_Inc._SBGI_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_112326093002_1795444202.html","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795444202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sinclair, Inc. (SBGI) \u2013 What Are Brokerages Saying About This Stock?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/sinclair-inc-sbgi-what-are-brokerages-saying-about-this-stock.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795171606.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sinclair (NASDAQ:SBGI) Stock: Insider Robert Weisbord Sells 10,000 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/15/sinclair-nasdaqsbgi-stock-insider-robert-weisbord-sells-10000-shares.html","date":"2026-11-15","timestamp":1794773965.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.922,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (SBGI) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/10/Price-Driven_Insight_from_SBGI_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_111326110401_1794585841.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794585841.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Texas TV Reporter Arrested for DWI, Found Allegedly Asleep in Car on Side of Highway","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/texas-tv-reporter-arrested-dwi-145541000.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795636702.0,"origin":"ti